  "notes": "The interest/consent state machine and the SRS-MAT-007 identifier. derivations: match_id = SHA-256(MATCH_ID_KDF_INFO | lower | higher)[:MATCH_ID_LEN] over the two peer ids in lexicographic byte order - symmetric, so both sides of an accept-accept race derive the same id with no message; initiator_on_race is the lower id. scripts: event timelines starting at state none; consumers replay each and compare state and effect after every step. Effects accept_and_establish and match_established are the ONLY unlocking effects (SRS-MAT-005); no decline or ignore step anywhere carries a transmitting effect (SRS-MAT-004); absorbed duplicates and reorders appear as steps whose state and effect repeat unchanged (SRS-MAT-014).",
